WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.480
A weaver's poet.

2
00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:04.670
Six ideas that still hold.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.270
Look within.

4
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.590
Where do you seek Me, the poem

5
00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.270
asks. I am beside you.

6
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.890
Not in temple or mosque, not in

7
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.170
rites. A true seeker sees Me in

8
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.080
a moment.

9
00:00:18.658 --> 00:00:20.158
The moon inside.

10
00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:23.118
The moon shines in my body, and

11
00:00:23.118 --> 00:00:25.538
my blind eyes cannot see it.

12
00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:28.158
The light is within, and we look

13
00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:29.668
right past it.

14
00:00:30.121 --> 00:00:31.121
The musk deer.

15
00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:34.001
The musk is in the deer, yet

16
00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:35.921
it wanders the forest hunting

17
00:00:35.921 --> 00:00:38.021
for the scent it carries.

18
00:00:38.021 --> 00:00:40.021
A very busy way to miss the

19
00:00:40.021 --> 00:00:40.821
point.

20
00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:43.649
One God, many names.

21
00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:46.229
Allah, Ram, Karim, Keshav.

22
00:00:46.229 --> 00:00:48.369
Gold is shaped into rings and

23
00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:50.829
bangles, yet is it not gold all

24
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:51.609
the same?

25
00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:53.999
The distinctions are only words.

26
00:00:54.505 --> 00:00:56.585
Neither temple nor mosque.

27
00:00:56.585 --> 00:00:59.645
If God lives only in the mosque,

28
00:00:59.645 --> 00:01:01.765
whose is the rest of the world?

29
00:01:01.765 --> 00:01:04.265
If in the idol, who knows what

30
00:01:04.265 --> 00:01:05.725
happens outside?

31
00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:08.035
Look into your own heart.

32
00:01:08.548 --> 00:01:10.508
Many hands, one name.

33
00:01:10.508 --> 00:01:12.608
His verses reached us in three

34
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:14.788
collections: the Bijak, the

35
00:01:14.788 --> 00:01:16.948
Kabir Granthavali, and the Adi

36
00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:19.268
Granth. Scholars cannot say for

37
00:01:19.268 --> 00:01:21.318
certain which lines are his.

38
00:01:22.453 --> 00:01:23.653
For GS1 and GS4:

39
00:01:23.653 --> 00:01:26.653
Kabir, nirguna bhakti, the sant

40
00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.733
bhasha, one God with many names,

41
00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:32.193
a questioning of empty ritual.

42
00:01:32.193 --> 00:01:35.713
Verses attributed to him, in the

43
00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:38.073
Bijak, the Granthavali and the

44
00:01:38.073 --> 00:01:39.123
Adi Granth.

45
00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:41.259
Look within.

46
00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:43.709
It is closer than you think.
